 - **Performance:** The loss aims to expedite training by adapting the number of Gaussian spheres according to scene complexity, thereby reducing thread idle periods during parallel pixel rendering [S1].
 - **Strengths:** Preserves reconstruction quality in complex regions while reducing computational load in simple regions. It adapts to scene complexity dynamically [S1].
-- **Limitations:** Requires access to gradient information or Gaussian counts per pixel during training. If gradients are noisy, the load balancing may be suboptimal.
